  / HASH-FORMAT-SHA-384-1 — inherit v7.66 AGILITY-ENTITY-1 corpus fixture
    (system/peer with 0xAA×64 pubkey, key_type='experimental-test' 0xFE).
    .1 pins the fixture's floor-form content_hash; .2 asserts that authoring
    that same fixture under content_hash_format=0x01 is REFUSED — V7 §4.5a
    item 1a pins system/peer to the floor unconditionally. See SEEDS.md §1.2. /

  {
    "id": "hash-format-sha-384.1.inherited_sha256_pin",
    "description": "v7.66 AGILITY-ENTITY-1 SHA-256-form content_hash for the (0xAA×64, 'experimental-test') fixture — the inherited cross-impl lock that anchors this vector",
    "kind": "inherited_corpus_pin",
    "input": {
      "type": "system/peer",
      "data": {
        "key_type":   "experimental-test",
        "public_key": h'aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa'
      },
      "content_hash_format": 0
    },
    "canonical_content_hash": h'003d0c34b508c5bf9eca5f086f09aac10f44bd43fca1a091b6aa55a096ca8fcd45',
    "source": "v7.66 §7.2 corpus pin; this vector inherits — no fresh seed"
  },

  {
    "id": "hash-format-sha-384.2.rehash",
    "description": "Authoring a system/peer under content_hash_format=0x01 (SHA-384) MUST be refused. V7 §4.5a item 1a (v7.77) pins the system/peer identity entity to the ECFv1-SHA-256 floor unconditionally — every connection, whatever the active format, whatever the peer's home format — because its data is wholly recoverable from the public peer-id and every consumer derives its hash rather than fetching it. A non-floor system/peer is therefore a construction that cannot exist, and this vector is the guard for the rule that retired it.",
    "kind": "construct_reject",
    "input": {
      "type": "system/peer",
      "data": {
        "key_type":   "experimental-test",
        "public_key": h'aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa'
      },
      "content_hash_format": 1
    },
    "expected_behavior": "construction refused. Error class is deliberately unspecified: this is a local authoring invariant, not a cross-peer seam, so two conformant impls cannot diverge observably across a peer boundary here — impls MAY use a structural validation error, and it is pinned only as 'the entity does not construct'. Same shape as varint-reserved-ff.1.key_type.",
    "verifier_requirement": "The refusal MUST be observed through the pinned peer-entity constructor. This vector previously asserted the OPPOSITE — that the rehash succeeds, pinning canonical_content_hash 012e64bbde3c494cf7cd… — and stayed green only because the verifier hand-built the entity instead of routing through the constructor that would have refused it. A fixture that exercises a forbidden construction and passes by bypassing the code that forbids it certifies the opposite of the rule (GUIDE-CONFORMANCE §2.4a failure shape).",
    "floor_form": "see hash-format-sha-384.1.inherited_sha256_pin — 003d0c34b5… is the only content_hash this fixture has"
  },

  / VARINT-MULTIBYTE-1 — multi-byte LEB128 format-code decode path exists +
    surfaces unsupported_content_hash_format for an unallocated integer.       /

  {
    "id": "varint-multibyte.1",
    "description": "system/hash with format-code bytes 80 01 (LEB128 of integer 128); impl decodes the multi-byte varint AND surfaces unsupported_content_hash_format (128 not in §1.2 seed table). Pins multi-byte LEB128 decoder existence.",
    "kind": "decode_reject",
    "input_format_code_varint": h'8001',
    "input_decoded_integer": 128,
    "expected_error_code": "unsupported_content_hash_format",
    "expected_status": 400
  },

  / VARINT-RESERVED-FF-1 — integer 255 reserved on both axes per §1.2 / §1.5. /

  {
    "id": "varint-reserved-ff.1.key_type",
    "description": "system/peer mint with key_type integer 255 (varint FF 01); impl MUST refuse — 255 reserved per V7 §1.5",
    "kind": "decode_reject",
    "input_key_type_varint": h'ff01',
    "input_decoded_integer": 255,
    "expected_behavior": "mint refused; error class unspecified (impls MAY use unsupported_key_type or a structural validation error; pinned only as: 'the entity does not construct')"
  },

  {
    "id": "varint-reserved-ff.2.hash_format",
    "description": "system/hash with format-code integer 255 (varint FF 01); MUST surface unsupported_content_hash_format",
    "kind": "decode_reject",
    "input_format_code_varint": h'ff01',
    "input_decoded_integer": 255,
    "expected_error_code": "unsupported_content_hash_format",
    "expected_status": 400
  },

  / FORMAT-CODE-INTERPRETATION-1 — unallocated single-byte format code →
    interpretation error (not a dispatch/routing miss). Renamed from v7.66
    PREFIX-DISPATCH-1 per the v7.68 §1.2 reframe.                              /

  {
    "id": "format-code-interpretation.1",
    "description": "system/hash with single-byte format-code 0x42 (unallocated); impl MUST surface unsupported_content_hash_format. The error is an INTERPRETATION error per V7 §1.2 v7.68 reframe — format-code is intrinsic to the hash, not a routing prefix.",
    "kind": "decode_reject",
    "input_format_code_byte": h'42',
    "expected_error_code": "unsupported_content_hash_format",
    "expected_status": 400
  },

  / ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── /
  / PHASE 2 — cross-key/cross-hash matrix (LOCKED, byte-pinned)              /
  / ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── /
  / The three matrix vectors share a structural shape: handshake → tree-get
    → cap grant A→B → cap use B→A. Per SEEDS.md §2.2, all three negotiate
    to active format SHA-256 (the standard-compliance fallback path).
    Per SEEDS.md §2.4, identity references use each peer's HOME format;
    cap-token content travels under the ACTIVE format. Per SEEDS.md §2.5,
    A's signature is over the cap-token's wire content_hash (RFC 8032
    deterministic).

    Phase-2 byte pins LOCKED from 3-way cohort round-trip
    (Go post-fix 3cfb353, Rust d38d1f8, Python a2463be — all byte-equal
    on the 7 gates: pubkeys, peer_ids, home content_hashes, cap-data
    CBOR, active cap content_hash, signature, .cbor sha256). Cohort
    closeouts recorded in the per-impl validation docs.

    Empty-scope dimension convention (arch ruling, see
    reviews/RULING-EMPTY-SCOPE-INCLUDE.md): an unconstrained
    scope dimension is present-with-empty-`include` `{include: []}`
    (CBOR `0x80`), NOT absent and NOT `{include: null}` (`0xf6`). Bound
    by ENTITY-CBOR-ENCODING §232 (fields MUST NOT be dropped) +
    §3.6 list-of(pattern) typing (null is not a valid value of a
    list field). The matrix `grants` entries below carry `handlers`
    and `operations` keys explicitly per this ruling.                          /

